x<0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85687901-9285-5cd2-a5f2-24299bd7d3d5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Intervals Given as Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067ab35d-3446-54d0-ab86-dccf2db05980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505117} {:answer/id #uuid "1288982b-1e41-5523-9287-ac0a98373888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505136} {:answer/id #uuid "288a4214-19f2-5d09-85fc-ef2a8e595f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505177} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8a424e-09b0-5a53-b8cf-b458e4c9e587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505355} {:answer/id #uuid "efca59c7-81ea-56a0-8aaf-ca437e657b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "067ab35d-3446-54d0-ab86-dccf2db05980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505117} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa662300-d1b2-51a6-b168-592189b59276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08faca23-bc00-55b8-ac21-ab67054edd09" :question/math-academy-id "q-44845" :question/problem "Given the inequalities $-3\\le x<2$ and $x<1$, express their common set of solutions as an interval." :question/worked-solution "We start by sketching the solutions to the two inequalities separately:\n\n![](images/72/7217f3db8adcbafdec9598e3c933fe1091e0abe9cabbdab57cca9cfb2d6cbb07.png)\n\n![](images/69/690bb39741f157b12583ffffb75e47bcc171e04b7082f09005025f333807a234.png)\n\nThe common set of values consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:\n\n![](images/d6/d6ab3f0c43897adf0ae1b063d4d1d2437ce6d8f08355ff9f07a1e3e861e451b3.png)\n\nTherefore, the common set of values is\n$[-3,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "630a6635-aac0-5627-82c8-8072b74dd8f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Intervals Given Graphically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f5bc00-d9be-599d-b79c-46034412f936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/89e7ca655d0769eb5441d5f73f6fc2e79f14705f6bfd4ea908a7a28afffb648f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505113} {:answer/id #uuid "335dd540-4b7a-56dd-9d43-c4989e173efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/ac1fe31a871c74052822ab50496d551759f0714650812c71d8000892ff87aa44.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505194} {:answer/id #uuid "5941c4e3-a0c6-58cb-9b74-6d8dcea6983d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/57/573a0ed4d14d765f1aa80929b32510eb4b28d101cf930df5c364dbab12999211.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505284} {:answer/id #uuid "651abdc4-ce28-59ef-8f8e-235432e6e3f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a2/a2665c9b1fe9a5fa3dd04081e00892e82a1a6990836b3f9c63ab08a19e6d51d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505309} {:answer/id #uuid "c591fc7a-6444-59f3-8234-bb53d1d0d072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :a